course: dictionary
lesson: 9470
title: What is a statement?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A statement is something you say or write that tells a fact or an idea. «A statement tells you something and usually ends with a full stop.» That is the easiest way to spot one in English.
explain: In grammar, there are four kinds of sentence: statements, questions, commands and exclamations. A statement tells something. A question asks something. A command tells someone to do something. An exclamation shows strong feeling.
explain: In maths, a statement can be checked as true or false. «All squares are rectangles» is a statement, and it is true. Some statements are the opposite, and you can check them.
explain: Statements also appear in real life. Mia's dad showed her a bank statement, which is a list of money going in and out of an account. Grown-ups check it for mistakes and fraud. An official statement from the Palace is a formal announcement that tells everyone a fact.
fact: A statement is something you say or write that tells a fact or an idea.
fact: In grammar, a statement is a sentence that tells something and ends with a full stop.
fact: In maths, a statement can be true or false: «All squares are rectangles» is true.
fact: A bank statement lists everything that went in and out of an account.
fact: A formal statement, like one from the Palace, is an official announcement.
exercise: Which sentence is a statement? | What a lovely surprise! | Close the door, please. | Are you ready for school? | *The sun rises in the east.
exercise: «A bank statement lists everything that went in and out of an account.» What does a bank statement show? | The times the bank is open | *Money going in and out of an account | A list of games to buy | Pictures of the bank building
exercise: In maths, «All squares are rectangles» is a statement. Is it true or false? | False | *True | Neither true nor false | It depends on the size of the square
test: In grammar, what is a statement? | A word that means a list | A sentence that shouts with excitement | A sentence that asks a question | *A sentence that tells something and ends with a full stop
test: «At the bottom are official statements from the Palace.» What is an official statement? | A secret whisper | *A formal announcement | A game with rules | A bill to pay at the shop
exam: Which of these is a statement that tells a fact? | *Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius at sea level. | Turn off the lights. | Why is the sky blue? | Oh, how lovely!
